1
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:12,920
Try stepping back and looking
at it in a brighter light.

2
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:28,620
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
my mom holding my hand.

4
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:42,440
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:47,700
So, on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I walked only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,800
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:09,080
Self-important politicians,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

10
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning at that corner.

11
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,900
You'll meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kame-ari surely it's Kame-ari.

13
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:33,060
Everyone, come on over to our town.

14
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:34,620
Thank you.

15
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:47,360
Reading that stupid manga on duty, you know.
Honestly.

16
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:50,700
Shut up, Ryo-chan.
You're always reading junk yourself.

17
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:54,520
This one is way more delicate than the stuff you read,
you know.

18
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:55,840
Let me see it.

19
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:58,380
It's gonna end happily anyway, right?

20
00:01:58,380 --> 00:01:59,620
Let's see, let's see.

21
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,800
A man and a woman who've just met...

22
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,300
...and actually the woman
has a one-sided crush,

23
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:06,660
and suddenly they kiss.

24
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:08,840
What a convenient story this is.

25
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:10,040
With this, even I could...

26
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:11,560
Especially since I'm married.

27
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,100
Exactly

28
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:15,740
Chief

29
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:16,940
Ryotsu

30
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:20,140
What do you think you're
doing reading manga on duty?

31
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,160
No, this is the thing is...

32
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:24,100
Don't blame others.

33
00:02:24,740 --> 00:02:26,600
That's a misunderstanding, Chief.

34
00:02:27,060 --> 00:02:29,700
What misunderstanding?
You were reading it right there!

35
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,380
Hey, Ryotsu.

36
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:33,920
The station chief wants you.

37
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:35,120
I came to get you.

38
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,420
The chief...

39
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:40,700
The chief summons you personally

40
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:43,200
He's not planning to fire you, is he?

41
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,800
I have no idea.

42
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,100
Anyway, let's go.

43
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,000
Hey, Ryotsu.

44
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,200
We'll have the farewell party
ready and waiting for you.

45
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,820
Mind your own business.

46
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:53,120
Let's go, pal.

47
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,600
You're going to get caught!

48
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:56,680
Come on!

49
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:10,500
What are you all gathering for?

50
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:12,980
It's Ryotsu and Kankichi!

51
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:23,000
What's the big idea, all of a sudden?

52
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,480
Even with all that, it's just too cruel.

53
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,280
That's right.

54
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:31,200
Trampling on Maria-chan's maiden heart
like that is the lowest of the low.

55
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:33,040
What are you talking about?

56
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,280
What's all this noise about?

57
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:38,940
Well, if it isn't Ryotsu. You're here.

58
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:40,620
Ryo-san.

59
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:43,460
Why, it's Sandy!

60
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,160
I've missed you.

61
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:48,540
No way

62
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:51,640
Why would a gorilla-like
guy get such a gorgeous blonde

63
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:54,740
Ryo-san, long time no see

64
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:57,960
Senpai, are you okay?

65
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:00,800
What do you think you're doing to Ryo-san?

66
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,600
What do you think you're doing?

67
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,040
Kissing my Ryo-sama like that!

68
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:06,720
My Ryo-sama?

69
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:10,020
Ryo-san, is this woman your girlfriend?

70
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:12,700
Maria isn't a girlfriend,

71
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:13,960
she's a boyfriend.

72
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:15,940
Boyfriend?

73
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:17,880
This person is a man.

74
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:20,260
Everyone's surprised at first

75
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:28,040
Sandy has that sort of taste? Maria's just
crushing on him all on her own. That's cruel!

76
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:34,520
Weren't the two of you living under the same roof?
I traveled with you too, you know!

77
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:39,600
Why on earth is Kankichi
so popular with women?

78
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:43,000
I can't understand how New York
foreigners and half-breeds think.

79
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:48,980
No, that's not it! Maria-kun,
Sandy-san, Ryotsu was in America...

80
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:50,932
When he went to America on a training trip,

81
00:04:50,982 --> 00:04:54,320
the New York City police officer
who looked after him in many ways.

82
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:57,375
In return, so to speak,

83
00:04:57,425 --> 00:05:01,760
this time he invited her to Katsushika
Police Station for training in Japan.

84
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:02,880
But...

85
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:06,433
What are you misunderstanding?
Drinking with Sandy until morning,

86
00:05:06,483 --> 00:05:09,760
I only escorted a witness
boy to the courthouse.

87
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:13,328
Is that so? How rude of me,

88
00:05:13,378 --> 00:05:15,160
what a misunderstanding that was.

89
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:17,080
Sandy's not blameless either, you know.

90
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:19,680
It's your fault for saying
such suggestive things.

91
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:20,840
So that's the thing -

92
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:23,360
Because Maria-san keeps getting so...

93
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,000
So that's what it was.

94
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:28,740
A gorgeous blonde like this...

95
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:30,240
Kankichi Ryotsu, from New York...

96
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,780
wouldn't come chasing after you all the way,
would she?

97
00:05:32,760 --> 00:05:33,820
So,

98
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:36,520
as the guide, Officer Ryotsu

99
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:38,260
as the representative
for the late-term training,

100
00:05:38,260 --> 00:05:41,360
I want Officer Honda to look after Sandy.

101
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:42,140
Understood.

102
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:49,280
Sandy, since you're free today,
shall we go sightseeing in Tokyo?

103
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:50,100
Yes.

104
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:55,220
Where would you like to see?
Tokyo Disneyland or Odaiba?

105
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:58,460
I love the old-town atmosphere of Tokyo.

106
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:00,520
Like Asakusa, for example.

107
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:04,160
Asakusa? That's my hometown.
My family home is there.

108
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,080
Really?

109
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:10,160
That's right, you can stay at my
family's home while you're here.

110
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:14,780
What's the problem, Sandy?

111
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:18,640
But I've already booked a hotel.

112
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:22,880
Cancel it, cancel it!
Let's spend the hotel money on a big party.

113
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:28,160
Well, that does sound more fun. OK.

114
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:31,780
Alright, it's settled.
Let's go sightseeing in Asakusa today!

115
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:35,720
So, that's the plan. Go hail a taxi.

116
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:36,560
Yes.

117
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:26,980
This really is a true old-town-style home,
isn't it?

118
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:30,520
It's a shack that's barely more than
a doghouse with a little fur on it.

119
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:32,960
Honda, thanks for your hard work.
You can go home now.

120
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:35,700
No, I'll be staying over too.

121
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:37,940
Why are you staying over too?

122
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:40,320
Maria asked me to.

123
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:43,040
to make sure nothing happens
between you and Sandy-san.

124
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,440
Yeah, as if something like
that would ever happen.

125
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:46,720
Hurry up and go home.

126
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:51,320
No way! I'm curious about Japan,
so I want to hear Sandy-san's stories too!

127
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:52,840
What's all the fuss about?

128
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:55,978
It's nothing. Can't be helped.

129
00:07:56,028 --> 00:07:58,800
My place is cramped,
so you'll be sleeping in the toilet.

130
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,460
Is anyone here?

131
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:08,200
It's Kankichi! What's going on?

132
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:10,900
I've brought a guest.

133
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:12,120
Sandy.

134
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:15,520
Hello, sorry for intruding.

135
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,400
Isn't that a foreigner?

136
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:20,680
I'll be imposing on this house for a while.

137
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,980
Sandy, don't be shy, come on in.

138
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:25,180
Dad, this is a big deal!

139
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:28,980
Kankichi brought a blonde person home!

140
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:29,820
Excuse me.

141
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:30,740
What?

142
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:36,280
Nice to meet you, I'm Sandy from New York.

143
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:38,740
Well, thank you very much for the welcome.

144
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:41,080
Kankichi, what is this all about?

145
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:43,720
What do you mean?
Can't you see for yourself?

146
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:46,620
Even so, bringing home a foreign bride!

147
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:49,240
Don't jump to conclusions, Sandy's a guy!

148
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:55,940
I see, so you're the police officer who
looked after you when you went to America?

149
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:59,060
I owe a debt for a night's lodging and a meal,
so leave it to me.

150
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:03,540
Your Japanese is very good,
and you're so polite too.

151
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:07,200
In America, I teach Japanese,
tea, and flower arranging.

152
00:09:07,940 --> 00:09:11,900
Hey Sandy, make yourself at home.
It's a dump, but don't stand on ceremony.

153
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:13,240
Mind your own business.

154
00:09:14,260 --> 00:09:17,840
That's right, it really is a dump,
but don't hold back.

155
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:22,460
Hey Sandy, aren't you hungry?

156
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:23,240
Well, yes.

157
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:26,440
Alright, Dad and Mom, let's eat.

158
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:30,700
Croquettes and menchi-katsu are okay, dear?

159
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:32,820
Idiot, she's a foreigner!

160
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:35,540
Of course foreigners eat
different food from Japanese people.

161
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:38,720
Kankichi, what do foreigners eat?

162
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,820
You went to America, didn't you?

163
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:45,320
Well, hamburger steak, bread,
and coffee should be fine, shouldn't they?

164
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,480
Mom, that's it. I'm counting on you.

165
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:54,080
We don't have anything like that.
Won't Ōchō and a kumade do, Dad?

166
00:09:54,500 --> 00:10:01,160
Don't be silly, she's not a mountain witch! Go buy it right away, it'll make it taste Japanese.
Alright then, I'll go.

167
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:13,060
Of course you'd say that, being back from America.
Well, I lived there for two weeks, so I'm practically American. Anyway, Dad's totally clueless about the world.

168
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:15,300
He doesn't even know where America is,
does he?

169
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,560
He doesn't get out much either, you know.

170
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:20,960
Look, let me explain using this croquette.

171
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:23,560
This is what Japan looks like.

172
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:26,180
This is Tokyo.

173
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:27,980
Dad's house is around here.

174
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:31,900
America is out past Hokkaido, right here.

175
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:34,000
That's pretty close.

176
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:36,720
I slept on the plane,
so I'm not really sure, but

177
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,220
we arrived in about an hour.

178
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:40,060
It's probably around here.

179
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:45,160
Wow! What a huge hamburger steak!

180
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:48,900
I can't vouch for the taste,
but it looks impressive, doesn't it?

181
00:10:49,300 --> 00:10:53,180
After all,
Mom has never made Western food before.

182
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:54,680
Well then, let's eat.

183
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:59,180
It's delicious, Mom.

184
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:01,880
Is that so? I'm glad you like it.

185
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:07,800
Is there something on my face?

186
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:08,987
No,

187
00:11:09,037 --> 00:11:12,960
I was just thinking how foreigners have blue eyes and look like dolls,
you know.

188
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,560
You're hopeless.

189
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:17,460
He's a pitiful, ignorant idiot of a father.

190
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:18,780
Well, don't mind him.

191
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:19,420
Come on.

192
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:24,100
He puts his own stupidity on a shelf and
lectures everyone like he's some big shot.

193
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:25,600
Suits you, you bastard!

194
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:28,380
Idiot, he takes after me, doesn't he?

195
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:29,920
You did it, you son of a gun, nice work!

196
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:32,500
Bring it on, then!

197
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:33,580
Ase-senpai!

198
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:36,000
Don't you dare make
that face at your mother!

199
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:40,120
No way!

200
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:41,460
You little...!

201
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:00,000
Stop it, you two!

202
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:03,080
If you're going to fight, take it outside!
You're bothering Sandy!

203
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:04,900
I can't go!

204
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:09,740
Don't worry, father-son fights are normal.
My father and brother do it all the time too.

205
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:12,980
They say the more you fight,
the closer you are, right?

206
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:18,280
So Japan and America are
no different after all.

207
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:21,820
You and Kan-chan go too far, you know.

208
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:48,360
What's with her riding so slowly?

209
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:50,180
What are you talking about?

210
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:54,140
Keeping your balance at low
speed takes serious skill.

211
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:57,840
She's speeding up.

212
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:05,160
What a bold ride.

213
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:07,340
She doesn't look like a woman at all.

214
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,780
That's a cornering turn!

215
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:14,760
Nice riding, Sandy.

216
00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:16,300
She's riding it effortlessly.

217
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:22,860
Amazing.

218
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:28,720
Wow! She stopped right before it!

219
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:30,700
Wow, that's amazing!

220
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:34,760
Japanese bikes are so easy to ride!
Very good!

221
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:38,020
Sandy-san, could you shake my hand?

222
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:40,220
I'd like your autograph, please.

223
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,760
Gladly!

224
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:44,422
Hold on! A handshake is 100 yen a time,

225
00:13:44,472 --> 00:13:45,980
and an autograph is 300 yen!

226
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:47,140
What?!

227
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,600
Y-Yone-san!

228
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:51,980
It's fine, it's fine.
This is a Japanese custom.

229
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:53,180
Phew.

230
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:57,452
Handshakes are 100 yen,
autographs are 300 yen,

231
00:13:57,502 --> 00:14:00,520
and a photo together is
now a special 500 yen!

232
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:01,600
What do you say, want in?

233
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,300
I want a picture!

234
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:04,500
Yeah, sure, sure!

235
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:05,440
That's it! This one!

236
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:06,100
Photo!

237
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:08,560
Handshakes and autographs,
so later, we'll do them.

238
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:10,060
Okay, don't push, don't push!

239
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:12,700
Anyone who's paid, please wait over there.

240
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:17,980
May you come a little closer?

241
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:19,160
Like this, is it?

242
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:21,980
Okay, next person!

243
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:25,060
Alright, smile more!

244
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:29,100
Senpai always rushes to make money,
you know.

245
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:32,520
But you two look great together,
Ryo-san and Sandy.

246
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:33,880
R-really?

247
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:39,340
Alright, Ryo-san, I'd like to
take a two-shot with you, Ryo-san.

248
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:40,142
W-well,

249
00:14:40,192 --> 00:14:43,600
Right, someone press the shutter for me.

250
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:44,080
Okay.

251
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,540
Well, I'm going now.

252
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,200
Hold on a second.

253
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:52,080
Please.

254
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,880
See, it looks good, right?

255
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:55,560
Yeah.

256
00:14:57,520 --> 00:14:58,067
Honda-san,

257
00:14:58,117 --> 00:15:01,580
shouldn't you play
Cupid for the two of them?

258
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:04,660
That's no good.
It wouldn't be fair to Maria-san.

259
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:09,320
Even if Maria-san likes Ryotsu-san,
isn't he a man?

260
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,000
Well, that's true.

261
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,140
Isn't Ryotsu-san our benefactor?

262
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:17,480
This time, Honda-san, you should be
the one to bring those two together.

263
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:19,480
Yeah, alright.

264
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:21,700
Alright.

265
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:25,680
Sandy-san, is there someone you like?

266
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:27,020
Well, yes.

267
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:29,160
What kind of person is he?

268
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,296
Well,

269
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:34,080
thick eyebrows,
a gorilla-like tough guy, you know.

270
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:39,820
That sounds like you, senpai.

271
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:43,280
And she's supposedly got
cockroach-like vitality.

272
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:44,700
Yes!

273
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:48,740
It's you after all, senpai!
This means there's hope!

274
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:54,060
Kankichi is her ideal type?

275
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:59,120
I think the person she said
she likes is you, senpai.

276
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:01,780
That must be some kind of mistake.

277
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:06,340
No, the way Sandy was gazing at
you had the eyes of a woman in love.

278
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:09,320
Dad, this might actually happen!

279
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:14,440
Well, if Sandy became Kankichi's
wife and came to live with us,

280
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:20,100
we could have her doing
all sorts of things for us.

281
00:16:21,420 --> 00:16:24,140
And then she'd help out
with the tsukudani too.

282
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:28,460
Father, could you do a taste test for me?

283
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:38,340
This is terrible.

284
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:44,360
It's far from the taste of 300 years.

285
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:46,140
Still too soft.

286
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:47,200
I'm so sorry.

287
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:48,280
Father.

288
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,560
Don't cry, Sandy.

289
00:16:53,540 --> 00:16:55,980
The road of tsukudani is long and hard.

290
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:58,340
Let's take it one step at a time, together.

291
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:00,400
Father.

292
00:17:01,040 --> 00:17:02,000
There, there.

293
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:06,040
I can't stop.

294
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,740
What weird thing are you imagining?

295
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:14,920
No, well...

296
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:19,360
Alright, Mom, go find out how Sandy feels.

297
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:22,000
I'll check how Honda-san and Kankichi feel.

298
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,240
Got it.

299
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:28,480
Hey, Sandy.

300
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:31,900
I'll ask you straight out:
do you like Kankichi?

301
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:33,800
Of course I do.

302
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:35,820
Really?

303
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:39,640
A wonderful man like him is rarely found.

304
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:44,060
Thanks for liking that idiot.

305
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:45,620
Mom.

306
00:17:46,340 --> 00:17:48,300
Ryotsu's my ideal type.

307
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:51,300
Yeah, Sandy said it plainly.

308
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:54,040
So what about your feelings?

309
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:58,740
Feelings? Well, I don't dislike him.
I mean, he's a foreigner, after all.

310
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:01,620
You idiot,
even if you searched the whole world,

311
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:04,300
there's no woman who'd
call you her ideal man!

312
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:05,320
Get married!

313
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:06,680
Marriage!

314
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:09,940
That's right,
you can definitely make it work!

315
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:12,620
Since we're at it,
why don't you just propose?

316
00:18:12,620 --> 00:18:14,880
Don't be ridiculous.

317
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:18,740
Sandy said she likes Kankichi!

318
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:21,100
I see.

319
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:25,700
Sandy, come over here and
show Kankichi your kimono!

320
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:39,660
What do you think, Ryo-san?

321
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:43,020
Y-you look really good on you.

322
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:44,240
I'm happy.

323
00:18:44,820 --> 00:18:46,020
No, you look sexy.

324
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:54,640
Maybe it's about time
for me to settle down too.

325
00:18:57,020 --> 00:18:58,740
Really? Is that true, senpai?

326
00:18:58,740 --> 00:19:01,620
It's not officially decided yet, though.

327
00:19:01,620 --> 00:19:05,540
No, since you two love each other,
it's practically decided already.

328
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:08,460
It's just like one of those manga you hate,
Ryo-chan.

329
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:11,500
Well, things like this happen in the world.

330
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:14,080
Alright, I'll be the matchmaker myself.

331
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:17,720
Are you all right? You have to give a speech in English,
you know.

332
00:19:18,110 --> 00:19:22,780
I see, I understand.
I'll make sure I'm ready by the ceremony.

333
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:24,960
Congratulations, senpai.

334
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:30,520
Only Americans can understand
a global man like me.

335
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:33,720
Hey, hey, Ryo-chan,
what did you say when you proposed?

336
00:19:35,540 --> 00:19:40,220
Nothing. Oh, that won't do.
Go propose to her right now!

337
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,660
That's right, senpai. Let's go!

338
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:54,060
Sandy? Dad took her out, saying he was going to look for a wedding venue.
I told him it was too early, but he went to look for one anyway.

339
00:19:54,060 --> 00:20:00,440
Oh-chan is so impatient, there's no helping it.
Let's go check on them

340
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:09,560
How about this place for you, Sandy?

341
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:10,820
What do you mean?

342
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:13,820
It's a wedding venue for Sandy and Kankichi.

343
00:20:15,080 --> 00:20:16,760
Stop it, Dad.

344
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:18,680
That's just a Japanese joke!

345
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,120
It's not a joke!

346
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:21,660
I'm dead serious.

347
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:23,780
I told you, senpai.

348
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:25,920
Go ahead and propose boldly, no hesitation.

349
00:20:28,740 --> 00:20:30,740
There's a minor actor in America.

350
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:33,040
But

351
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:35,680
But you said you liked Kankichi!

352
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:37,860
Not as a man,

353
00:20:37,910 --> 00:20:40,480
I meant I like him as a person.

354
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:44,440
N-no way...

355
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:46,760
Ohhhhhhh...

356
00:20:47,900 --> 00:20:48,920
Yeah, let's go.

357
00:20:50,780 --> 00:20:54,040
Sorry! It's all because
I jumped to conclusions...

358
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:59,320
Don't be ridiculous! I never planned
on marrying a blonde from the start!

359
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:01,000
Let's go.

360
00:21:01,580 --> 00:21:02,380
Senpai

361
00:21:03,460 --> 00:21:05,360
Honda, hurry up.

362
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:07,200
Let's go drinking tonight.

363
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:18,700
Tsukudani is all I have.

364
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:20,100
Sorry I don't have any souvenirs for you.

365
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:21,180
Not at all.

366
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:24,080
Thank you all so much.

367
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:26,200
Thank you very much

368
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:28,220
Give my regards to Chief Chakkiri.

369
00:21:28,220 --> 00:21:30,160
Please come again.

370
00:21:36,260 --> 00:21:38,280
Ryotsu isn't coming, Dad.

371
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:41,080
We got everyone so worked up, after all.

372
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:45,200
No, he's not the kind of guy who gets
discouraged by something like that.

373
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:49,680
But I'm his father,
so you can trust me on this.

374
00:21:52,620 --> 00:21:54,980
Aren't you supposed to be
heading to Narita, mister?

375
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,920
Just do as Mom says.

376
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:58,040
Understood.

377
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:06,860
Take care.

378
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:09,180
Be happy, okay?

379
00:22:13,860 --> 00:22:16,100
Ryotsu didn't show up after all

380
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:18,200
Yes, I've done something wrong.

381
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:27,400
Now, move like I told you.

382
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:30,140
Why do I have to do something like that?

383
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:32,360
Shut up.

384
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:34,800
I'll arrest you.

385
00:22:42,440 --> 00:22:44,720
So I'm really saying goodbye to Japan.

386
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:52,140
Bye.

387
00:22:53,900 --> 00:22:54,900
Ryotsu!

388
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:59,540
Ryo-san!

389
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,400
Thanks, Ryo-san.

390
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:09,540
Goodbye.

391
00:23:18,260 --> 00:23:18,960
Sandy

392
00:23:21,940 --> 00:23:24,375
You idiot!
Even though you're a police officer,

393
00:23:24,425 --> 00:23:27,620
who stops cars on the expressway like that!

394
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:29,440
It's out now, though.

395
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:30,840
Ryo-sama!

396
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:35,886
Ryo-sama! Even though I'm right here,

397
00:23:35,936 --> 00:23:37,940
how could you marry someone else?
That's cruel!

398
00:23:38,240 --> 00:23:39,980
W-wait! It's a misunderstanding!

399
00:23:40,580 --> 00:23:41,680
I won't forgive you!

400
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:42,920
Those guys!

401
00:23:44,120 --> 00:23:45,300
It's nothing!

402
00:23:45,300 --> 00:23:47,180
Just run away!

403
00:23:47,180 --> 00:23:48,940
Wait!

404
00:23:48,940 --> 00:23:52,320
Both of you, three months' suspension!

405
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:53,120
Yeah.

406
00:24:15,300 --> 00:24:19,500
On the train, your back to the road home,
you're sure to fall asleep,

407
00:24:20,540 --> 00:24:25,800
another hard week done,
overwork is only natural,

408
00:24:27,060 --> 00:24:30,500
bucket in hand, looking all composed,

409
00:24:30,500 --> 00:24:33,320
beef bowl with extra sauce,
"tsuyudaku" style,

410
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:36,580
the irritation of endless overtime,

411
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:40,200
irritation cleared away in one go.

412
00:25:00,720 --> 00:25:08,740
Thank you for watching.

413
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:26,100
Monday

414
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:53,660
Thank you for watching.

